vtsatip - authors and credits
=============================

Copyright (C) 2026 Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
  Author and maintainer of vtsatip. The plugin was written with the help of
  Claude (Anthropic), an AI assistant, under his direction.

vtsatip builds on the work of others. Without them it would not exist:

SAT>IP plugin for VDR
  https://github.com/FireFlyVDR/vdr-plugin-satip
  Originally written by Rolf Ahrenberg (https://github.com/rofafor/vdr-plugin-satip),
  now maintained by the FireFlyVDR project. GPLv2.
  Used in vtsatip: param.c/param.h (channel parameters -> SAT>IP URL
  parameters) taken with small changes, the software section filter
  (sectionfilter.c/.h) adapted, the overall structure of device, setup menu
  and plugin class, and the collection of server quirks (reports from users
  such as Christian Wick for the FRITZ!WLAN Repeater DVB-C and Dirk Wagner for
  the Telestar Digibit R1, as credited in the HISTORY of that plugin).
  The section reassembly follows the Linux dvb_demux code.

vtuner-ng
  https://github.com/joed74/vtuner-ng
  Maintained by Jochen Dolze (joed74); the satip daemon is Copyright (C) 2014
  mc.fishdish@gmail.com; vtuner-ng is based on vtuner by Honza Petrous
  (Copyright (C) 2010-2012). GPLv2.
  Used in vtsatip: the control flow (one persistent RTSP session, one PLAY
  per retune with the complete PID list, standard PIDs, lock on the first TS
  packet, dropping stale packets, realtime RTP thread) and the way the
  SAT>IP query is built. No code was copied; the behaviour was reimplemented.

VDR (Video Disk Recorder)
  Klaus Schmidinger, https://www.tvdr.de - the plugin API, and the plugin
  example Makefile this Makefile follows. GPLv2.

SAT>IP protocol specification
  SES Astra / the SAT>IP Consortium - the protocol and the x_pmt/x_ci CI
  extension as implemented by Digital Devices (OctopusNet) and minisatip.

License
